Other peaks in the Sentinel Range had previously been named for John Evans and William Long . Later ascents ( edit ) Gavin Bate ascending Mount Vinson in 2000 The climb of Vinson offers little technical difficulty beyond the usual hazards of travel in Antarctica , and as one of the Seven Summits , it has received much attention from well - funded climbers in recent years . Multiple guide companies offer guided expeditions to Mount Vinson , at a typical cost of around $30,000 per person , including transportation to Antarctica from Chile . First ascent from east side ( edit ) While the vast majority of prior climbs to the summit have used the western side of the massif from the Branscomb Glacier , the first ascent from the east side was successfully completed by an eight - person team sponsored by NOVA in January 2001 . The team consisted of : Conrad Anker -- expedition leader Jon Krakauer -- mountaineer and author Dave Hahn -- mountain guide with 34 ascents , including ascents to Gardner , and Shinn .","entities":["Sentinel Range","Vinson Massif","Branscomb Glacier","John Evans","William Long","Gavin Bate","NOVA","eight-person team","Conrad Anker","Jon Krakauer","Dave Hahn","Shinn","Ascent of Mount Vinson","First ascent from the east side","Seven Summits"],"facts":["Vinson Massif summit plateau -LOCATED_IN-> Sentinel Range","Vinson Massif & The Sentinel Range: New map -- new names -RELATED_TO-> Sentinel Range","flight into the Sentinel Range -RELATED_TO-> Sentinel Range","C-130 Hercules -RELATED_TO-> Sentinel Range","Sentinel Range -PART_OF-> Ellsworth Mountains"]}
