[E8001fa] {"title":"Fundamental rights in India","text":"Fundamental rights in India
A notable development during that period having significant effect on the Indian constitution took place on 10 December 1948 when the United Nations General Assembly adopted the Universal Declaration of Human Rights and called upon all member states to adopt these rights in their respective constitutions . The fundamental rights were included in the First Draft Constitution ( February 1948 ) , the Second Draft Constitution ( 17 October 1948 ) and final Third Draft Constitution ( 26 November 1949 ) , prepared by the Drafting Committee . Significance and characteristics ( edit ) The fundamental rights were included in the constitution because they were considered essential for the development of the personality of every individual and to preserve human dignity . The writers of the constitution regarded democracy of no avail if civil liberties , like freedom of speech and religion were not recognised and protected by the State . According to them , `` democracy '' is , in essence , a government by opinion and therefore , the means of formulating public opinion should be secured to the people of a democratic nation . For this purpose , the constitution guaranteed to all the citizens of India the freedom of speech and expression and various other freedoms in the form of the fundamental rights .","entities":["Universal Declaration of Human Rights","human dignity","Fundamental Rights","Adoption of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights","Drafting Committee","First Draft Constitution","Second Draft Constitution","Third Draft Constitution","civil liberties","freedom of speech","Freedom of speech and expression","Indian constitution","India","personality","religion"],"facts":["Universal Declaration of Human Rights -RELATED_TO-> Human rights","Fundamental Rights -RELATED_TO-> Union List","Cyrus Cylinder -RELATED_TO-> Universal Declaration of Human Rights","Cyrus Cylinder -RELATED_TO-> human dignity","Fundamental Rights -RELATED_TO-> State List"]}
