African Footballer of the Year - wikipedia African Footballer of the Year Jump to : navigation , search The African Footballer of the Year award , presented to the best African footballer each year , has been conferred by the Confederation of African Football ( CAF ) since 1992 . An earlier African Footballer of the Year Golden Ball award was given out between 1970 and 1994 by France Football magazine . The changes resulted in parallel Golden Ball awards given out to Abedi Pele and George Weah in 1993 and 1994 by the magazine although the CAF sponsored awards for those years were won respectively by Rashidi Yekini and Emmanuel Amuneke , as well as two awards given to Abedi Pelé in 1992 . France Football discontinued the election from 1995 after the European Ballon d'Or -- also awarded by the magazine -- had been opened to all players in the European leagues . On 2 February 2008 , Sevilla 's Frédéric Kanouté was named the 2007 African Footballer of the Year .","entities":["African Footballer of the Year award","African Footballer of the Year Golden Ball award","France Football","Emmanuel Amuneke","European Ballon d'Or","European leagues","George Weah","Abedi Pele","Rashidi Yekini","Frédéric Kanouté","Confederation of African Football"],"facts":["George Weah -RELATED_TO-> African Footballer of the Year","George Weah -RELATED_TO-> football","France Football -RELATED_TO-> African Footballer of the Year","African Footballer of the Year -RELATED_TO-> France Football","George Weah -RELATED_TO-> Sub-Saharan Africa"]}
