He is dethroned by the spectre of an actor , and we shall never be able to keep the usurper out of our dreams . Maurice Maeterlinck in La Jeune Belgique ( 1890 ) . Shakespeare 's day to the Interregnum ( edit ) Shakespeare almost certainly wrote the role of Hamlet for Richard Burbage . He was the chief tragedian of the Lord Chamberlain 's Men , with a capacious memory for lines and a wide emotional range . Judging by the number of reprints , Hamlet appears to have been Shakespeare 's fourth most popular play during his lifetime -- only Henry IV Part 1 , Richard III and Pericles eclipsed it . Shakespeare provides no clear indication of when his play is set ; however , as Elizabethan actors performed at the Globe in contemporary dress on minimal sets , this would not have affected the staging . Firm evidence for specific early performances of the play is scant .","entities":["Lord Chamberlain's Men","Maurice Maeterlinck","La Jeune Belgique","Henry IV Part 1","Richard Burbage","Shakespeare","Richard III","Hamlet","Pericles","globe"],"facts":["Richard Burbage -RELATED_TO-> groundlings","Richard Burbage -RELATED_TO-> Othello","Richard Burbage -RELATED_TO-> Hieronimo","Richard Burbage -RELATED_TO-> Lear","Hattaway -RELATED_TO-> Richard Burbage"]}
[Ed7ccd2] {"title":"Hamlet","text":"Hamlet
In the 400 years since its inception , the role has been performed by numerous highly acclaimed actors in each successive century . Three different early versions of the play are extant : the First Quarto ( Q1 , 1603 ) ; the Second Quarto ( Q2 , 1604 ) ; and the First Folio ( F1 , 1623 ) . Each version includes lines and entire scenes missing from the others . The play 's structure and depth of characterisation have inspired much critical scrutiny . One such example is the centuries - old debate about Hamlet 's hesitation to kill his uncle , which some see as merely a plot device to prolong the action , but which others argue is a dramatisation of the complex philosophical and ethical issues that surround cold - blooded murder , calculated revenge , and thwarted desire . More recently , psychoanalytic critics have examined Hamlet 's unconscious desires , while feminist critics have re-evaluated and attempted to rehabilitate the often maligned characters of Ophelia and Gertrude . Contents ( hide ) 1 Characters 2 Plot 2.1 Act I 2.2 Act II 2.3 Act III 2.","entities":["Gertrude","First Quarto","Second Quarto","First Folio","Ophelia","Hamlet"],"facts":["Gertrude -RELATED_TO-> Guildenstern","Gertrude -RELATED_TO-> ghost","Gertrude -RELATED_TO-> Hamlet","Gertrude -RELATED_TO-> Poisoned glass of wine","Gertrude -LOCATED_IN-> Denmark"]}
