The Sea of Monsters - wikipedia The Sea of Monsters Jump to : navigation , search This article is about the Percy Jackson novel . For other uses , see Sea of Monsters ( disambiguation ) . The Sea of Monsters Cover of unknown later US edition with Rocco illustration ( same as first ed . ) Author Rick Riordan Cover artist John Rocco ( depicted ) Country United States Series Percy Jackson & the Olympians ( book 2 ) Genre Fantasy , Greek mythology , young - adult novel Published April 1 , 2006 Publisher Miramax Books and Disney Hyperion Media type Print ( hardcover and paperback ) , audiobook , e-book Pages 279 pp . ISBN 0 - 7868 - 5686 - 6 OCLC 64664383 LC Class MLCS 2006 / 45756 ( P ) Preceded by The Lightning Thief Followed by The Titan 's Curse The Sea of Monsters is a fantasy - adventure novel based on Greek mythology written by Rick Riordan and published in 2006 . It is the second novel in the Percy Jackson & the Olympians series and the sequel to The Lightning Thief .","entities":["United States","The Sea of Monsters","John Rocco","Disney Hyperion","young-adult novel","The Lightning Thief","Miramax Books","Rick Riordan","The Titan's Curse","Percy Jackson & the Olympians","Greek mythology","fantasy"],"facts":["United States -PART_OF-> Americas","United States -PART_OF-> Northern America","United States -PART_OF-> these ten countries","United States -PART_OF-> The Americas","United States -PART_OF-> Beekeeping by countries"]}
[E38ebb3] {"title":"The Sea of Monsters","text":"The Sea of Monsters
This book chronicles the adventures of thirteen - year - old demigod Percy Jackson as he and his friends rescue his satyr friend Grover from the Cyclops Polyphemus and save the camp from a Titan 's attack by bringing the Golden Fleece to cure Thalia 's poisoned pine tree . The Sea of Monsters was released on April 1 , 2006 , by Miramax Books , an imprint of Hyperion Books for Children and thus Disney Publishing ( succeeded by the Disney Hyperion imprint ) . It was generally well -- received and was nominated for numerous awards , including the 2006 Book Sense Top Ten Summer Pick and the 2009 Mark Twain Award . It sold over 100,000 copies in paperback with over one million copies total and was released in audiobook format on September 6 , 2006 . The Sea of Monsters is followed by The Titan 's Curse , the third book of the five in the series . A film adaptation of the book , Percy Jackson : Sea of Monsters , was released on August 7 , 2013 .","entities":["The Sea of Monsters","Disney Hyperion","the camp","Thalia's poisoned pine tree","Titan's attack","Miramax Books","Hyperion Books for Children","Disney Publishing","2006 Book Sense Top Ten Summer Pick","2009 Mark Twain Award","Grover","Golden Fleece","Polyphemus","Percy Jackson","The Sea of Monsters audiobook"],"facts":["The Sea of Monsters -RELATED_TO-> Films","The Sea of Monsters -LOCATED_IN-> United States","The Sea of Monsters -RELATED_TO-> young-adult novel","The Sea of Monsters -RELATED_TO-> The Lightning Thief","The Sea of Monsters -RELATED_TO-> Tyson"]}
[E8fb7ff] {"title":"The Sea of Monsters","text":"The Sea of Monsters
Percy gives her the Fleece that she takes to Camp Half Blood . Polyphemus wishes to wed her after it is revealed to him that Grover is a male satyr . Luke Castellan : The main antagonist , now 20 ; he works for Kronos . He captures Percy and the rest before being thwarted by Chiron and his brethren , the Party Ponies . Tyson the Cyclops : Percy 's half brother ; he is initially portrayed as a homeless child before Annabeth helps Percy realize that he is a Cyclops . He accompanies Percy and Annabeth in their quest and befriends a hippocampus whom he names Rainbow . He is very big and has one brown eye . When Clarisse 's ship explodes , he is presumed dead until it is learned that he survived due to his immunity to fire . Critical reception ( edit ) The Sea of Monsters received generally positive reviews with reviewers praising the storyline , the themes and the author 's style of writing . `` In a feat worthy of his heroic subjects , Riordan crafts a sequel stronger than his compelling debut , '' said a Publishers Weekly review .","entities":["The Sea of Monsters","Kronos","Annabeth","Grover","Tyson","Luke Castellan","Clarisse","Percy","fleece","Polyphemus","Chiron","Party Ponies","Camp Half Blood","Rainbow","Riordan"],"facts":["The Sea of Monsters -RELATED_TO-> Films","The Sea of Monsters -RELATED_TO-> Disney Hyperion","The Sea of Monsters -RELATED_TO-> young-adult novel","The Sea of Monsters -RELATED_TO-> The Lightning Thief","The Sea of Monsters -LOCATED_IN-> United States"]}
