Similar penalties may apply to an income tax return ( Form 1120S ) for an S corporation return . 100 % penalty on unpaid withholding taxes ( edit ) Employers are required to withhold income and social security taxes from wages paid to employees , and to pay these amounts promptly to the government . A penalty of 100 % of the amount not paid over ( plus liability for paying the withheld amounts ) may be collected without judicial proceedings from each and every person who had custody and control of the funds and did not make the payment to the government . This applies to company employees and officers as individuals , as well as to companies themselves . There have been reported cases of the IRS seizing houses of those failing to pay over employee taxes . Penalties for failure to provide foreign information ( edit ) Taxpayers who are shareholders of controlled foreign corporations must file Form 5471 with respect to each such controlled foreign corporation . Penalties for failure to timely file are $10,000 to $50,000 per form , plus possible loss of foreign tax credits . U.S.","entities":["IRS","income tax return","Form 1120S","S corporation","100% penalty on unpaid withholding taxes","withholding taxes","social security taxes","persons with custody and control of the funds","houses","controlled foreign corporations","taxpayers","Form 5471","penalties for failure to timely file","foreign tax credits","company officers"],"facts":["IRS -RELATED_TO-> IRS penalties","IRS -RELATED_TO-> audit","IRS -RELATED_TO-> IRS notice","IRS -RELATED_TO-> tax","IRS -RELATED_TO-> business loan"]}
