Qualifications for the Judges ( a ) He should be a citizen of India . ( b ) He should have been ( I ) a judge for 10 years of Subordinate court under the Judicial Service of the State or ( ii ) an Advocate for 10 years in a High Courts in India ( Article 217 ) . Tenure : Originally the age of the retirement of the judges of the High Courts was fixed at 60 but it was raised to 62 in 1963 according to the 15th amendment of the Constitution . Removal of the Judges : A judge may leave his office by resigning . He will send his letter of resignation to the President . His office would be considered to have been vacated if he is appointed as a judge of the Supreme Court or is transferred to some other High Court . A judge of a High Court may also be removed like a judge of the Supreme Court . A judge of High Court may be removed by the President if the Parliament passes a motion against him by an absolute majority and 2 / 3rd majority of the members present and voting , both the Houses sitting separately .","entities":["constitution","president","India","High Courts","Indian High Courts Act 1861","Judicial Service of the State","the State","Subordinate court","Advocate","Article 217","15th amendment of the Constitution","judge","motion against a judge","Parliament","Supreme Court"],"facts":["constitution -RELATED_TO-> Begar","constitution -RELATED_TO-> Religions","constitution -RELATED_TO-> rights of minorities","constitution -RELATED_TO-> litigation","constitution -RELATED_TO-> Untouchability"]}
