Both hypertension and diabetes mellitus can cause damage to the tiny blood vessels that supply the retina , leading to hypertensive retinopathy and diabetic retinopathy . Retinoblastoma is a cancer of the retina . Retinal diseases in dogs include retinal dysplasia , progressive retinal atrophy , and sudden acquired retinal degeneration . Lipemia retinalis is a white appearance of the retina , and can occur by lipid deposition in lipoprotein lipase deficiency . Diagnosis ( edit ) A number of different instruments are available for the diagnosis of diseases and disorders affecting the retina . Ophthalmoscopy and fundus photography have long been used to examine the retina . Recently , adaptive optics has been used to image individual rods and cones in the living human retina , and a company based in Scotland has engineered technology that allows physicians to observe the complete retina without any discomfort to patients . The electroretinogram is used to non-invasively measure the retina 's electrical activity , which is affected by certain diseases . A relatively new technology , now becoming widely available , is optical coherence tomography ( OCT ) .","entities":["Dogs","rods","cones","hypertension","hypertensive retinopathy","diabetic retinopathy","retinoblastoma","retinal diseases","retinal dysplasia","progressive retinal atrophy","sudden acquired retinal degeneration","lipemia retinalis","lipid deposition","lipoprotein lipase deficiency","fundus photography"],"facts":["Dogs -RELATED_TO-> visual streak","Dogs -RELATED_TO-> Matthew 7:6","Dogs -RELATED_TO-> burial pits","Hops -RELATED_TO-> Dogs","15-kilohertz high-frequency tone -RELATED_TO-> Dogs"]}
