When mature the haploid ovule produces the female gamete which are ready for fertilization . The male haploid is pollen and is produced by the anther , when pollen lands on a mature stigma of a flower it grows a pollen tube down into the flower . The haploid pollen then produces sperm by mitosis and releases them for fertilization . Notes and references ( edit ) Jump up ^ `` gamete '' . Online Etymology Dictionary . Jump up ^ Marshall , A.M. 1893 . Vertebrate embryology : a text - book for students and practitioners . GP Putnam 's Sons . Jump up ^ Yeung , C. , M. Anapolski , M. Depenbusch , M. Zitzmann , and T. Cooper . 2003 . `` Human sperm volume regulation . Response to physiological changes in osmolality , channel blockers and potential sperm osmolytes . '' Human Reproduction 18 : 1029 . ^ Jump up to : Jay Phelan ( 30 April 2009 ) . What Is Life ? : A Guide to Biology W / Prep - U . Macmillan . pp.","entities":["Online Etymology Dictionary","fertilization","mitosis","Gamete","sperm","ovule","Pollen","Anther","Stigma","Flower","Pollen tube","gamete","A.M. Marshall","Vertebrate embryology: a text-book for students and practitioners","GP Putnam's Sons"],"facts":["Douglas Harper -RELATED_TO-> Online Etymology Dictionary","Baccalaureate -RELATED_TO-> Online Etymology Dictionary","Meritocracy -RELATED_TO-> Online Etymology Dictionary","Photosynthesis -RELATED_TO-> Online Etymology Dictionary","bond -PART_OF-> Online Etymology Dictionary"]}
