A similar event occurred in Boscastle , England , on 16 August 2004 . Hazards ( edit ) Each year , many people are killed or seriously injured by severe thunderstorms despite the advance warning . While severe thunderstorms are most common in the spring and summer , they can occur at just about any time of the year . Cloud - to - ground lightning ( edit ) See also : Lightning strike and Wildfire A return stroke , cloud - to - ground lightning strike during a thunderstorm . Cloud - to - ground lightning frequently occurs within the phenomena of thunderstorms and have numerous hazards towards landscapes and populations . One of the more significant hazards lightning can pose is the wildfires they are capable of igniting . Under a regime of low precipitation ( LP ) thunderstorms , where little precipitation is present , rainfall can not prevent fires from starting when vegetation is dry as lightning produces a concentrated amount of extreme heat . Direct damage caused by lightning strikes occurs on occasion . In areas with a high frequency for cloud - to - ground lightning , like Florida , lightning causes several fatalities per year , most commonly to people working outside . Acid rain is also a frequent risk produced by lightning .","entities":["Vegetation","England","Florida","severe thunderstorms","Boscastle","A similar event","cloud-to-ground lightning","lightning strike","wildfires","low precipitation thunderstorms","fires","Acid rain","Thunderstorm","precipitation"],"facts":["Vegetation -RELATED_TO-> savannahs","Vegetation -RELATED_TO-> montane land","Vegetation -RELATED_TO-> Kruger National Park","oil spills -RELATED_TO-> Vegetation","Vegetation -RELATED_TO-> forests"]}
