The race was won by the George Hanlon trained 40 - 1 outsider Piping Lane ridden by John Letts and carrying only 48 kg . 1985 -- The first sponsored Melbourne Cup , and the first million dollar Cup , with $650,000 for the winner . 1987 -- First female jockey to ride in the cup was Maree Lyndon on Argonaut Style . Dunaden : 2011 Melbourne Cup winner , painted by Charles Church 1993 -- The Dermot Weld trained Irish gelding Vintage Crop became the first Northern hemisphere trained horse to win the Melbourne Cup and the first Irish horse . 2001 -- Sheila Laxon , was the first woman trainer to officially win the Melbourne Cup . However , Mrs. A. McDonald ( 1938 ) with Catalogue was really the first woman trainer to win . Women then could not be registered as trainers in Australia , and it was her husband who was the registered trainer . Mrs. McDonald 's win was as a female trainer of a female owned horse . 2003 -- First Australian female jockey to ride in the cup was Clare Lindop on Debben .","entities":["1985 Melbourne Cup","Sheila Laxon","1987 Melbourne Cup","1993 Melbourne Cup","2001 Melbourne Cup","1938 Melbourne Cup","2003 Melbourne Cup","2011 Melbourne Cup","George Hanlon","Piping Lane","John Letts","Maree Lyndon","Argonaut Style","Dunaden","Charles Church"],"facts":["1985 Melbourne Cup -LOCATED_IN-> Australia","2011 Melbourne Cup -RELATED_TO-> Racing Victoria","Sheila Laxon -RELATED_TO-> Ethereal","What a Nuisance -RELATED_TO-> 1985 Melbourne Cup","Mrs. Allan McDonald -RELATED_TO-> Catalogue"]}
