dantrolene ) , so this name is inaccurate . Most sources still use the term `` centrally acting muscle relaxant '' . According to MeSH , dantrolene is usually classified as a centrally acting muscle relaxant . The World Health Organization , in its ATC , uses the term `` centrally acting agents '' , but adds a distinct category of `` directly acting agents '' , for dantrolene . Use of this terminology dates back to at least 1973 . The term `` spasmolytic '' is also considered a synonym for antispasmodic . Clinical use ( edit ) Spasmolytics such as carisoprodol , cyclobenzaprine , metaxalone , and methocarbamol are commonly prescribed for low back pain or neck pain , fibromyalgia , tension headaches and myofascial pain syndrome . However , they are not recommended as first - line agents ; in acute low back pain , they are not more effective than paracetamol or nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs ( NSAIDs ) , and in fibromyalgia they are not more effective than antidepressants .","entities":["World Health Organization","Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs","Antispasmodic","cyclobenzaprine","methocarbamol","dantrolene","MeSH","ATC","centrally acting muscle relaxant","centrally acting agents","directly acting agents","spasmolytic","Spasmolytics","low back pain","acute low back pain"],"facts":["World Health Organization -RELATED_TO-> Speed control","World Health Organization -RELATED_TO-> Ebola vaccine","World Health Organization -RELATED_TO-> Bamako Initiative conference","World Health Organization -RELATED_TO-> Indian government","World Health Organization -LOCATED_IN-> Geneva"]}
