Products ( edit ) Zara stores have men 's and women 's clothing , as well as children 's clothing ( Zara Kids ) . Zara 's products are supplied based on consumer trends . Its highly responsive supply chain ships new products to stores twice a week . After products are designed , they take ten to fifteen days to reach the stores . All of the clothing is processed through the distribution center in Spain . New items are inspected , sorted , tagged , and loaded into trucks . In most cases , the clothing is delivered within 48 hours . Zara produces over 450 million items per year . Manufacturing and distribution ( edit ) Zara Almere - Heren The men 's department of a typical Zara store . Almere , Netherlands Zara clothing made in Portugal Zara store in New York City . Zara store in Brisbane Zara store in Palma de Mallorca ( Spain ) . Zara store in Brussels ( Belgium ) . Reportedly , Zara needs just one week to develop a new product and get it to stores , compared to the six - month industry average , and launches around 12,000 new designs each year .","entities":["Brussels","New York City","Belgium","Portugal","Spain","Netherlands","Zara Kids","Zara clothing","distribution center","Almere","Palma de Mallorca","Zara","Brisbane"],"facts":["Brussels -LOCATED_IN-> Flanders","Parliament of the Brussels Capital Region -LOCATED_IN-> Brussels","Toyota Europe -LOCATED_IN-> Brussels","German driver becomes Toyota's millionth hybrid customer in Europe, goes home with two Auris Hybrids -LOCATED_IN-> Brussels","ACEA -LOCATED_IN-> Brussels"]}
