[Ea62538] {"title":"Country Music Hall of Fame and Museum","text":"Country Music Hall of Fame and Museum
Award recipients are determined through a two - stage balloting process ; the first round of voting narrows each category to five candidates ; the second round selects winners . The large select committee of electors that votes on Hall of Fame membership is composed of CMA members who have participated in the country music industry for at least ten years . New Hall of Fame members receive special recognition in ceremonies at the Country Music Hall of Fame and Museum . Bas - relief portraits cast in bronze honoring each Hall of Fame member were originally displayed at the Tennessee State Museum in downtown Nashville until the Country Music Hall of Fame and Museum opened its own building in April 1967 ; in this barn - roofed facility at the head of Music Row , the bronze plaques comprised a special exhibit . Today the plaques are displayed in a seventy - foot - high rotunda at the museum 's enlarged downtown Nashville facility . The museum collection ( edit ) The museum 's archival and library storage , allows for the cultivation of the museum 's collection and includes more than 2.5 million artifacts .","entities":["artifacts","Music Row","CMA","country music industry","Tennessee State Museum","bronze plaques","museum collection","opening of the museum's own building","Rotunda","Country Music Hall of Fame and Museum","Nashville"],"facts":["British Museum -RELATED_TO-> artifacts","Three-age -RELATED_TO-> artifacts","Three-stage system -RELATED_TO-> artifacts","lithic reduction -RELATED_TO-> artifacts","Historic RCA Studio B -LOCATED_IN-> Music Row"]}
