[Ef5c5d9] {"title":"Migration in China","text":"Migration in China
However , in the mid-2000s attitudes towards migration drastically changed . In the novel Out to work , Migration , Gender , and the Changing Lives of Rural Women in Contemporary China , Gaetano explained how `` Migrants were finally recognized to be critical in narrowing the rural - urban income gap , as they redistribute wealth through remittances and apply new knowledge and skills to develop rural areas '' . Even though China recognized the importance of migrant workers , their `` low levels of education , skills , and work experience , and their dearth of urban social connections , combined with the hukou - based job distribution '' still created many disadvantages for rural migrants . Social impacts ( edit ) Labor supply ( edit ) In general , the current system of circular migration of floating populations in China offers greater labor resources to coastal areas of high economic activity , but `` although labor productivity in migrant activities is higher than it is in local nonfarm sectors , the current economic cost of migration in China is so high as to significantly limit such reallocation . The current system therefore works to reduce the overall productivity of labor and causes a tremendous loss of social resources . ''","entities":["gender","China","migrant workers","Labor supply","Migration","Gaetano","Out to work, Migration, Gender, and the Changing Lives of Rural Women in Contemporary China","rural migrants","hukou-based job distribution","circular migration","floating populations","coastal areas"],"facts":["gender -RELATED_TO-> Gender division of labor","prohibition of discrimination -RELATED_TO-> gender","Sir Gawain and the Green Knight -RELATED_TO-> gender","Succession to the Crown Act 2013 -RELATED_TO-> gender","gender -RELATED_TO-> colonial ideals"]}
