Measurement of high voltages is possible by the potential transformers . Combined instrument transformer ( edit ) Combined instrument transformer A combined instrument transformer encloses a current transformer and a voltage transformer in the same transformer . There are two main combined current and voltage transformer designs : oil - paper insulated and SF insulated . One advantage of applying this solution is reduced substation footprint , due to reduced number of transformers in a bay , supporting structures and connections as well as lower costs for civil works , transportation and installation . Pulse transformer ( edit ) Bothhand TS6121A pulse transformer A pulse transformer is a transformer that is optimised for transmitting rectangular electrical pulses ( that is , pulses with fast rise and fall times and a relatively constant amplitude ) . Small versions called signal types are used in digital logic and telecommunications circuits , often for matching logic drivers to transmission lines . Medium - sized power versions are used in power - control circuits such as camera flash controllers . Larger power versions are used in the electrical power distribution industry to interface low - voltage control circuitry to the high - voltage gates of power semiconductors .","entities":["Current transformer","Voltage transformer","potential transformers","high voltages","combined instrument transformer","oil-paper insulated","SF insulated","Bothhand TS6121A pulse transformer","pulse transformer","electrical pulses","signal types","digital logic","telecommunications circuits","logic drivers","transmission lines"],"facts":["Current transformer -PART_OF-> Instrument transformer","combined instrument transformer -PART_OF-> Instrument transformer","transformer -RELATED_TO-> Voltage transformer","Voltage transformer -PART_OF-> Instrument transformer","Transformer types -RELATED_TO-> electrical transformer"]}
