The Gift of the Magi - wikipedia The Gift of the Magi Jump to : navigation , search This article is about the short story . For the Magi that visited baby Jesus , see Biblical Magi . For other uses , see The Gift of the Magi ( disambiguation ) . `` The Gift of the Magi '' Author O. Henry Country United states Language English Genre ( s ) Short story Published in The Four Million Publication type Anthology Publication date December 10 , 1905 ( newspaper ) ; April 10 , 1906 ( book ) `` The Gift of the Magi '' is a short story , written by O. Henry ( a pen name for William Sydney Porter ) , about a young husband and wife and how they deal with the challenge of buying secret Christmas gifts for each other with very little money . As a sentimental story with a moral lesson about gift - giving , it has been a popular one for adaptation , especially for presentation at Christmas time . The plot and its twist ending are well - known , and the ending is generally considered an example of comic irony . It was allegedly written at Pete 's Tavern on Irving Place in New York City .","entities":["United States","New York City","English","The Four Million","Pete's Tavern","Irving Place","The Gift of the Magi","O. Henry","Short story"],"facts":["United States -PART_OF-> Americas","United States -PART_OF-> Northern America","United States -PART_OF-> these ten countries","United States -PART_OF-> The Americas","United States -PART_OF-> Beekeeping by countries"]}
[E3bcd98] {"title":"The Gift of the Magi","text":"The Gift of the Magi
Unusually late , Jim walks in and immediately stops short at the sight of Della , who had previously prayed that she was still pretty to Jim . Della then admits to Jim that she sold her hair to buy him his present . Jim gives Della her present -- an assortment of combs , useless now that her hair is short . Della then shows Jim the chain she bought for him , to which Jim says he sold his watch to get the money to buy her combs . Although Jim and Della are now left with gifts that neither one can use , they realize how far they are willing to go to show their love for each other , and how priceless their love really is . The story ends with the narrator comparing the pair 's mutually sacrificial gifts of love with those of the Biblical Magi .","entities":["hair","gifts","Biblical Magi","chain","Della","Jim","assortment of combs","watch","love","The Gift of the Magi","the narrator"],"facts":["Maximus -RELATED_TO-> hair","magical black rock spikes -RELATED_TO-> hair","Eugene -RELATED_TO-> hair","Pascal -RELATED_TO-> hair","Rapunzel -RELATED_TO-> hair"]}
[E7be09c] {"title":"The Gift of the Magi","text":"The Gift of the Magi
It was allegedly written at Pete 's Tavern on Irving Place in New York City . The story was initially published in The New York Sunday World under the title `` Gifts of the Magi '' on December 10 , 1905 . It was first published in book form in the O. Henry Anthology The Four Million in April 1906 . Contents ( hide ) 1 Summary 2 Adaptations 3 References 4 External links Summary ( edit ) Mr. James Dillingham Young ( `` Jim '' ) and his wife , Della , are a couple living in a modest apartment . On Christmas Eve , with only $1.87 in hand , and desperate to find a gift for Jim , Della sells her hair for $20 to a nearby hairdresser named Madame Sofronie , and eventually finds a platinum pocket watch fob chain for Jim 's watch for $21 . Satisfied with the perfect gift for Jim , Della runs home and begins to prepare pork chops for dinner . At 7 o'clock , Della sits at a table near the door , waiting for Jim to come home .","entities":["New York City","The Four Million","Pete's Tavern","Irving Place","The New York Sunday World","Initial publication of The Gift of the Magi","Publication of The Gift of the Magi in book form","James Dillingham Young","Della","Madame Sofronie","modest apartment","Della's hair","platinum pocket watch fob chain","Jim's watch","The Gift of the Magi"],"facts":["New York City -LOCATED_IN-> New Jersey","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> New York","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> New York (state)","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> North America","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> United States"]}
[Eeae2a6] {"title":"The Gift of the Magi","text":"The Gift of the Magi
Adaptations ( edit ) The story has been adapted to films , The Sacrifice ( 1909 ) , Love 's Surprises Are Futile ( 1916 ) , The Gift of the Magi ( 1917 ) , a segment of O. Henry 's Full House ( 1952 ) , The Gift of Love ( 1978 ) , The Gift of the Magi ( 1958 ) , Dary magów ( Poland , 1972 ) , Christmas Eve on Sesame Street ( 1978 ) , I 'll not be a gangster , love ( Не буду гангстером , дорогая / Nebūsiu gangsteriu , brangioji , USSR , 1978 ) , Mickey 's Once Upon a Christmas ( 1999 ) , The Gift of the Magi ( 2004 ) and the short film for the Irish band The Script in 2010 called For the First Time . Love , another French movie , based some of its scenes on this story . Raincoat ( 2004 ) , a Hindi film directed by Rituparno Ghosh is an adaptation of the story .","entities":["The Script","The Gift of the Magi","The Sacrifice","Love's Surprises Are Futile","O. Henry's Full House","The Gift of Love","Dary magów","Christmas Eve on Sesame Street","I'll not be a gangster, love","Mickey's Once Upon a Christmas","For the First Time","Raincoat","Rituparno Ghosh","Love"],"facts":["The Script -CREATED-> Man On A Wire","The Gift of the Magi -RELATED_TO-> HBO","The Gift of the Magi -RELATED_TO-> United States","The Gift of the Magi -RELATED_TO-> English","The Gift of the Magi -RELATED_TO-> Wikisource"]}
