He played a young deputy Billy Norris , in The Big Valley episode `` The Other Face Of Justice '' in 1969 . While enlisted in the United States Army for two years , Crawford worked on training films as a production coordinator , assistant director , script supervisor , and occasional actor . His rank was sergeant at the time of his honorable discharge in December 1967 . In 1968 , Crawford played a soldier wanted for murder in `` By the Numbers '' , an episode of the popular TV series Hawaii Five - O . The Resurrection of Broncho Billy was a USC student film Crawford agreed to do as a favor to his close friend , producer John Longenecker . It won the 1970 Academy Award for Best Live Action Short Subject . The Naked Ape was a partially animated 1973 feature film starring Crawford and Victoria Principal , produced by Hugh Hefner . In 1976 , Johnny Crawford co-starred as Ben Shelby in the tenth episode of season three of Little House on the Prairie , `` The Hunters '' . In 1985 , Crawford appeared as Noah Paisley , sheriff 's deputy , in an episode of Murder , She Wrote .","entities":["United States Army","Billy Norris","The Big Valley","The Other Face Of Justice","honorable discharge","soldier wanted for murder","Hawaii Five-O","By the Numbers","The Resurrection of Broncho Billy","John Longenecker","Academy Award for Best Live Action Short Subject","The Naked Ape","Victoria Principal","Hugh Hefner","Little House on the Prairie"],"facts":["United States Army -RELATED_TO-> Indian Defence Ministry's 1965 report","United States Army -RELATED_TO-> Wilson","United States Army -RELATED_TO-> German Army","United States Army -RELATED_TO-> National Guard","United States Army -LOCATED_IN-> United States"]}
