Both remember how good with a gun Dude used to be . Chance 's friend Pat Wheeler ( Ward Bond ) and his wagon train of supplies stop in town , with a young gunslinger , Colorado Ryan ( Ricky Nelson ) , riding guard . Inside the jail , Stumpy ( Walter Brennan ) , Chance 's game - legged deputy , keeps watch over the jail and Joe , who knows that Stumpy holds an old grudge against Joe 's wealthy and powerful brother . Joe warns his jailers that Nathan Burdette will not like how his brother is being treated . A mysterious woman nicknamed Feathers ( Angie Dickinson ) is in the saloon , playing poker . In the meantime , Dude and Chance patrol the town . Hotel owner Carlos ( Pedro Gonzalez - Gonzalez ) stops the sheriff , saying Wheeler has been talking too much about Chance needing help . In the saloon , Chance implores Wheeler to stop , as it will draw attention from the wrong people . Wheeler suggests that Colorado could be of assistance , but Colorado politely declines , saying he wants to `` mind my own business '' . Colorado also promises not to start any trouble without telling the sheriff first .","entities":["Carlos","Rio Bravo","Pat Wheeler","Colorado Ryan","Stumpy","Pedro Gonzalez-Gonzalez","Chance","Feathers","Nathan Burdette","Dude","Angie Dickinson","Ricky Nelson","Walter Brennan","Ward Bond","Joe"],"facts":["Carlos -RELATED_TO-> Amuzegar","Carlos -RELATED_TO-> Houari Boumédienne","Carlos -RELATED_TO-> plane","Carlos -RELATED_TO-> ransom","Carlos -RELATED_TO-> Yamani"]}
