The 6,900 - square - metre ( 1.7 - acre ) harbor basin was built from 1897 to 1898 when the section of the canal ( the then branch channel of the Dortmund - Ems Canal ) , was already flooded . In 1912 , at the colliery port handled 360,096 tonnes of goods . In 1913 the docks expanded . Because of mining subsidence by 1954 the quaywall had to be increased by 2.50 metres ( 8.2 ft ) . In the 1980s , it was leased to Automobil - und Motorbootsport - Club Castrop - Rauxel e . V ( The car and motorboat club of Castrop - Rauxel ) and is used from recreational boating , being no longer used by Ruhrkohle AG , and contains many small boats . The former mine railway , which starts at the harbour is now a walking and biking trail .","entities":["Dortmund–Ems Canal","harbor basin","colliery port","docks","quaywall","Automobil- und Motorbootsport-Club Castrop-Rauxel e. V.","Castrop-Rauxel","Ruhrkohle AG","former mine railway","walking and biking trail","harbor basin construction","goods handling at the colliery port","docks expansion","quaywall increase","lease to the club"],"facts":["Rhine–Herne Canal -LOCATED_IN-> Germany","Rhine–Herne Canal -LOCATED_IN-> Ruhr area","Port Victor -LOCATED_IN-> Castrop-Rauxel","former mine railway -RELATED_TO-> walking and biking trail","Rhine–Herne Canal -LOCATED_IN-> Duisburg"]}
