The industrial port is ~ 900 by 60 metres ( 2,950 by 200 ft ) and the trading port ~ 500 by 75 metres ( 1,640 by 246 ft ) . A private railway of length 18.4 kilometres ( 11.4 mi ) is operated which is linked to the tracks of the Deutsche Bahn Formerly the port dealt mainly with coal and mining products , now the port is a major hub for petroleum products and second - largest inland port for cereals in North Rhine - Westphalia . It is operated by the Gelsenkirchener Logistik - , Hafen - und Servicegesellschaft ( Gelsenkirchener logistics , harbour and service company . ) a subsidiary of Stadtwerke Gelsenkirchen . Port Grimberg ( edit ) The port at Grimberg Hafen Grimberg ( Port Grimberg ) is on the south canal bank in Gelsenkirchen , near the city boundary to Herne . It was named after the nearby Castle Grimberg , of which today only the foundations remain .","entities":["Gelsenkirchen","Gelsenkirchener Logistik-, Hafen- und Servicegesellschaft","Stadtwerke Gelsenkirchen","Port Grimberg","Castle Grimberg","Rhine–Herne Canal","Herne"],"facts":["Rhine–Herne Canal -LOCATED_IN-> Germany","lock at Gelsenkirchen -LOCATED_IN-> Gelsenkirchen","City port of Gelsenkirchen -LOCATED_IN-> Gelsenkirchen","Pump station at Gelsenkirchen -LOCATED_IN-> Gelsenkirchen","Rhine–Herne Canal -LOCATED_IN-> Ruhr area"]}
