( In a later book of the series , The Tin Woodman of Oz , the woman is said to be the Witch 's servant , and it is the Witch herself who decides to enchant Nick 's axe . ) The enchanted axe chopped off his limbs , one by one . Each time he lost a limb , Ku - Klip the tinsmith replaced it with a prosthetic limb made of tin . Finally , nothing was left of him but tin . However , Ku - Klip neglected to replace his heart . Once Nick Chopper was made entirely of tin , he was no longer able to love the lady he had fallen for . In The Wonderful Wizard of Oz , Dorothy Gale befriends the Tin Woodman after they find him rusted in the forest , as he was caught in rain , and use his oil can to release him . He follows her to the Emerald City to get a heart from The Wizard . They are joined on their adventure by the Scarecrow and the Cowardly Lion . The Wizard sends Dorothy and her friends to the Winkie Country to kill the Wicked Witch of the West .","entities":["axe","Heart","forest","Tin Woodman","Ku-Klip","Witch","The Wonderful Wizard of Oz","Dorothy Gale","Emerald City","The Wizard","Scarecrow","Cowardly Lion","Winkie Country","Wicked Witch of the West","prosthetic limb"],"facts":["axe -RELATED_TO-> Beauty and the Beast: The Enchanted Christmas","the Green Knight -RELATED_TO-> axe","Green Knight -RELATED_TO-> axe","Jeff Bennett -RELATED_TO-> axe","axe -RELATED_TO-> Gawain"]}
