The movie was made available for free viewing online and free downloading of its soundtrack . In the 2013 prequel , Oz the Great and Powerful , although the Tin Woodman does not physically appear , the film introduces his creator , the Master Tinker , portrayed by Bill Cobbs . Tin Man appears in the animated film Legends of Oz : Dorothy 's Return ( which is based on Dorothy of Oz ) , voiced by Kelsey Grammer . The Woodsman , a 2012 stage play written by James Ortiz with music by Edward W. Hardy , tells the backstory of the Tin Man , using puppetry , movement , and music . The play has received multiple Off Broadway productions , and won a 2016 Obie Award for Ortiz 's puppet design . In the TV series Emerald City , the Tin Woodman equivalent is Jack ( Gerran Howell ) , a friend of the enigmatic Tip , who helps ' him ' escape from his imprisonment by a witch . When it is revealed that Tip is actually a girl whose true identity was suppressed by a potion , her strained emotional state causes her to push Jack over a balcony after he kisses her .","entities":["Jack","Tin Woodman","Witch","Oz the Great and Powerful","Master Tinker","Bill Cobbs","Legends of Oz: Dorothy's Return","Dorothy of Oz","Kelsey Grammer","The Woodsman","James Ortiz","Edward W. Hardy","Off Broadway productions","Obie Award","puppet design"],"facts":["Jack -LOCATED_IN-> Coal Valley","Jack -LOCATED_IN-> Hope Valley","Jack -LOCATED_IN-> Downton Abbey","Jack -LOCATED_IN-> servants' hall","Jack -LOCATED_IN-> Hamilton"]}
