He was named after a swimming pool in Paris , despite the fact that neither his mother nor his father particularly liked swimming . The story is told as a narrative from the perspective of a middle - aged Pi , now married with his own family , and living in Canada . At the time of main events of the story , he is sixteen years old . He recounts the story of his life and his 227 - day journey on a lifeboat when his ship sinks in the middle of the Pacific Ocean during a voyage to North America . Richard Parker ( edit ) A Bengal tiger Richard Parker is a royal Bengal tiger who is stranded on the lifeboat with Pi when the ship sinks . Richard Parker lives on the lifeboat with Pi and is kept alive with the food and water Pi delivers . Richard Parker develops a relationship with Pi that allows them to coexist in their struggle . In the novel , a hunter named Richard Parker is hired to kill a panther thought to have killed seven people within two months . Instead , he accidentally immobilizes a female Bengal tiger with tranquilizer darts while her cub escapes hiding in a bush . Parker names the cub Thirsty after his enthusiasm when drinking from a nearby river .","entities":["Pacific Ocean","panther","Pi","lifeboat","Richard Parker","female Bengal tiger","Thirsty","Life of Pi","North America","Canada"],"facts":["Papahānaumokuākea Marine National Monument -LOCATED_IN-> Pacific Ocean","Mauna Kea -LOCATED_IN-> Pacific Ocean","Bikini Atoll -LOCATED_IN-> Pacific Ocean","Ring of Fire -LOCATED_IN-> Pacific Ocean","tropical storms -LOCATED_IN-> Pacific Ocean"]}
