The flip - up LCD display 's resolution was 640x200 pixels . Bondwell 2 also included MicroPro 's complete line of CP / M software , including WordStar . The Bondwell 2 was capable of displaying bitmapped graphics . The price of the Bondwell 2 was listed at $995 . Compaq portable ( edit ) The Compaq Portable was the first portable computer created in 1982 which one of the first 100 % IBM PC compatible systems . The first shipment was in March 1983 and was priced at $2,995 . The Compaq Portable folded up into a luggable case the size of a portable sewing machine . The third model of this development , Compaq Portable II , featured high resolution graphics on its tube display . It was the first portable computer ready to be used on the shop floor , and for CAD and diagram display . It established Compaq as a major brand on the market . Epson HX - 20 ( edit ) Epson HX - 20 ( 1981 ) Epson L3s ( ~ 1990 ? )","entities":["IBM PC","Bondwell 2","CP/M","MicroPro","WordStar","Compaq Portable","Compaq Portable II","Compaq","CAD","Epson L3s","Epson HX-20"],"facts":["IBM PC -RELATED_TO-> Code page 437","Bondwell 2 -RELATED_TO-> 3.5 '' floppy disk drive","IBM -RELATED_TO-> IBM PC","Bondwell 2 -RELATED_TO-> Z-80 CPU","Bondwell 2 -RELATED_TO-> LCD display"]}
