Above this shrine is the painting Last Supper by the lesser - known Giovanni Balducci . There was also a glass - paste mosaic panel The Bust of Saint Zanobius by the 16th - century miniaturist Monte di Giovanni , but it is now on display in the Museum Opera del Duomo . Many decorations date from the 16th - century patronage of the Grand Dukes , such as the pavement in colored marble , attributed to Baccio d'Agnolo and Francesco da Sangallo ( 1520 -- 26 ) . Some pieces of marble from the façade were used , topside down , in the flooring ( as was shown by the restoration of the floor after the 1966 flooding ) . It was suggested that the interior of the 45 metre ( 147 ft ) wide dome should be covered with a mosaic decoration to make the most of the available light coming through the circular windows of the drum and through the lantern . Brunelleschi had proposed the vault to glimmer with resplendent gold , but his death in 1446 put an end to this project , and the walls of the dome were whitewashed .","entities":["vault","lantern","dome","Brunelleschi","Museum Opera del Duomo","Baccio d'Agnolo","façade","Saint Zanobius","Last Supper","Giovanni Balducci","The Bust of Saint Zanobius","Monte di Giovanni","Grand Dukes","pavement in colored marble","Francesco da Sangallo"],"facts":["lantern -RELATED_TO-> farmhouse fire","Sir Francis Drake -RELATED_TO-> vault","vault -RELATED_TO-> gold treasure","vault -LOCATED_IN-> Oak Island","lantern -RELATED_TO-> coffee table"]}
