This is because the wheel has to be stored clear of the ground when the vehicle is in road - going mode - Such wheels can be as small as 245 mm ( 9.65 in ) in diameter . In Australia , wheels for Road - rail vehicles should comply with the requirements of AS7514. 4 which is the standard for infrastructure maintenance vehicle wheels . Tire ( edit ) Main article : Railway tire The wheels of many rail vehicles , especially steam locomotives and older types of rolling stock are fitted with steel tires ( or tyres in British English , Australian English and others ) to provide a replaceable wearing element on a costly wheel . These steel tires should not be confused with the tires fitted to rubber - tyred metros and people movers , for example some lines of the Paris Métro , the Mexico City Metro , the Caracas Metro , the Montreal Metro , Sapporo Subway , Seattle Center Monorail , Taipei Rapid Transit System and the Santiago Metro . Tire installation ( edit ) Steel tire on a steam locomotive 's driving wheel is heated with gas flames to expand and loosen it so it may be slipped over the wheel .","entities":["Australia","road-going mode","Road-rail vehicle","AS7514.4","Infrastructure maintenance vehicle wheels","Rail vehicles","Steam locomotive","Rolling stock","Railway tire","Steel tire","Rubber-tyred metro","People mover","Paris Métro","Mexico City Metro","Caracas Metro"],"facts":["Australia -PART_OF-> Cairns Group","Australia -PART_OF-> British Empire","Australia -PART_OF-> Northern Territory","Australia -PART_OF-> Tasmania","Australia -PART_OF-> Jervis Bay Territory"]}
